{
  "info": {
    "name": "qBittorrent TV Renamer — Part 2: Rename Files",
    "_postman_id": "qbt-tv-part2-rename-files",
    "description": "Part 2 of 2 — re-fetches the torrent file list (now under the renamed root from Part 1), builds a rename queue, then loops renameFile for every episode.\n\nCONFIG: Edit the collection variables before running:\n  qbtBaseUrl   — e.g. http://localhost:8080\n  username     — qBittorrent Web UI username\n  password     — qBittorrent Web UI password\n  torrentHash  — same hash used in Part 1\n  showName     — same show name used in Part 1 (e.g. Arcana)\n  seasonFolder — season sub-folder (e.g. Season 01)\n  mode         — \"dry\" to preview only (default) | \"apply\" to actually rename files\n\nEach request logs in via the Web API before running.\nIMPORTANT: Run this collection via the Collection Runner.\nIn dry mode, request 3 prints the full rename plan and stops — request 4 is skipped.\nChange mode to \"apply\" and re-run to commit all renames.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "qbtBaseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "description": "Base URL of qBittorrent Web UI (no trailing slash)"
    },
    {
      "key": "username",
      "value": "",
      "description": "qBittorrent Web UI username (REQUIRED)"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "",
      "type": "secret",
      "description": "qBittorrent Web UI password (REQUIRED)"
    },
    {
      "key": "torrentHash",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Hash of the torrent to rename (REQUIRED — same as Part 1)"
    },
    {
      "key": "showName",
      "value": "Arcana",
      "description": "Show name — must match what was used in Part 1 (it is now the root folder name)"
    },
    {
      "key": "seasonFolder",
      "value": "Season 01",
      "description": "Season sub-folder placed inside the root (e.g. Season 01)"
    },
    {
      "key": "fileRenameQueue",
      "value": "[]",
      "description": "Auto-populated by request 3 — JSON array of {oldPath, newPath} objects"
    },
    {
      "key": "fileRenameIndex",
      "value": "0",
      "description": "Loop counter managed automatically by request 4 — do not edit"
    },
    {
      "key": "currentOldPath",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Current file oldPath for the active loop iteration — do not edit"
    },
    {
      "key": "currentNewPath",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Current file newPath for the active loop iteration — do not edit"
    },
    {
      "key": "mode",
      "value": "dry",
      "description": "\"dry\" = preview only, prints plan and stops (default) | \"apply\" = actually rename all files"
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const baseUrl = (pm.collectionVariables.get('qbtBaseUrl') || '').replace(/\\/+$/, '');",
          "const username = pm.collectionVariables.get('username');",
          "const password = pm.collectionVariables.get('password');",
          "",
          "if (!baseUrl) {",
          "    throw new Error('Set the qbtBaseUrl collection variable before running.');",
          "}",
          "if (!username || !String(username).trim()) {",
          "    throw new Error('Set the username collection variable before running.');",
          "}",
          "if (password === undefined || password === null || password === '') {",
          "    throw new Error('Set the password collection variable before running.');",
          "}",
          "",
          "const loginRequest = {",
          "    url: baseUrl + '/api/v2/auth/login',",
          "    method: 'POST',",
          "    header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },",
          "    body: {",
          "        mode: 'urlencoded',",
          "        urlencoded: [",
          "            { key: 'username', value: String(username) },",
          "            { key: 'password', value: String(password) }",
          "        ]",
          "    }",
          "};",
          "",
          "pm.sendRequest(loginRequest, (err, res) => {",
          "    if (err) {",
          "        throw new Error('Login request failed: ' + err.message);",
          "    }",
          "    const body = res.text();",
          "    if (res.code !== 200 || body !== 'Ok.') {",
          "        throw new Error('qBittorrent login failed (' + res.code + '): ' + body);",
          "    }",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "3. Get Torrent Files (build rename queue)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Reset loop state before rebuilding the queue",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('fileRenameIndex', '0');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('fileRenameQueue', '[]');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('currentOldPath', '');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('currentNewPath', '');",
              "",
              "const hash = pm.collectionVariables.get('torrentHash');",
              "if (!hash || !hash.trim()) {",
              "    throw new Error('Set the torrentHash collection variable before running.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Response is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const files = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('File list is non-empty', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(Array.isArray(files) && files.length > 0).to.be.true;",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (!Array.isArray(files) || files.length === 0) {",
              "    throw new Error('Empty or invalid file list — check torrentHash.');",
              "}",
              "",
              "const showName     = pm.collectionVariables.get('showName');",
              "const seasonFolder = pm.collectionVariables.get('seasonFolder');",
              "",
              "// Helper: extract SxxExx from a filename",
              "function episodeFromBasename(basename) {",
              "    const m = basename.match(/S(\\d{1,2})E(\\d{1,2})/i);",
              "    if (!m) return null;",
              "    return {",
              "        season:  m[1].padStart(2, '0'),",
              "        episode: m[2].padStart(2, '0')",
              "    };",
              "}",
              "",
              "// Re-detect root from the current (post-Part-1) paths; fall back to showName",
              "const roots = new Set();",
              "for (const f of files) {",
              "    const i = f.name.indexOf('/');",
              "    if (i !== -1) roots.add(f.name.slice(0, i));",
              "}",
              "const currentRoot = roots.size === 1 ? [...roots][0] : showName;",
              "",
              "// Build the rename queue",
              "const queue   = [];",
              "const skipped = [];",
              "",
              "for (const f of files) {",
              "    const rel  = f.name;",
              "    const base = rel.split('/').pop();",
              "",
              "    // Skip .nfo sidecar files (mirrors original script behaviour)",
              "    if (/\\.nfo$/i.test(base)) {",
              "        skipped.push({ reason: '.nfo — skipped', path: rel });",
              "        continue;",
              "    }",
              "",
              "    const ep = episodeFromBasename(base);",
              "    if (!ep) {",
              "        skipped.push({ reason: 'no SxxExx pattern found', path: rel });",
              "        continue;",
              "    }",
              "",
              "    const ext     = base.includes('.') ? base.slice(base.lastIndexOf('.') + 1) : '';",
              "    const newFile = showName + ' S' + ep.season + 'E' + ep.episode + '.' + ext;",
              "    const newPath = currentRoot + '/' + seasonFolder + '/' + newFile;",
              "",
              "    queue.push({ oldPath: rel, newPath: newPath });",
              "}",
              "",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('fileRenameQueue', JSON.stringify(queue));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('fileRenameIndex', '0');",
              "",
              "pm.test('At least one episode queued for rename', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(queue.length).to.be.greaterThan(0,",
              "        'No SxxExx episode files found — check show files or season pattern.');",
              "});",
              "",
              "console.log('Detected root folder :', currentRoot);",
              "console.log('Season sub-folder    :', seasonFolder);",
              "console.log('Episodes queued      :', queue.length);",
              "console.log('Skipped              :', skipped.length);",
              "if (skipped.length) {",
              "    console.log(JSON.stringify(skipped, null, 2));",
              "}",
              "console.log('');",
              "console.log('Full rename plan:');",
              "console.log(JSON.stringify(queue, null, 2));",
              "console.log('');",
              "",
              "const mode = (pm.collectionVariables.get('mode') || 'dry').trim().toLowerCase();",
              "",
              "if (mode === 'dry') {",
              "    console.log('MODE: DRY RUN — no files will be renamed.');",
              "    console.log('Review the plan above, then change mode to \"apply\" and re-run.');",
              "    pm.execution.setNextRequest(null);",
              "} else {",
              "    console.log('MODE: APPLY — starting file renames now...');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{qbtBaseUrl}}/api/v2/torrents/files?hash={{torrentHash}}",
          "host": ["{{qbtBaseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "v2", "torrents", "files"],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "hash",
              "value": "{{torrentHash}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Re-fetches the file list now that the root folder has already been renamed by Part 1. Builds the full rename queue (stored in {{fileRenameQueue}}) and prints the plan to the console before any file is touched. Resets the loop counter to 0."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Rename Episode File (loop)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const queue = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('fileRenameQueue') || '[]');",
              "const index = parseInt(pm.collectionVariables.get('fileRenameIndex') || '0', 10);",
              "",
              "if (queue.length === 0) {",
              "    throw new Error('fileRenameQueue is empty — run request 3 first to build the queue.');",
              "}",
              "",
              "if (index >= queue.length) {",
              "    // Past the end — test script will stop the runner",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('currentOldPath', '');",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('currentNewPath', '');",
              "} else {",
              "    const step = queue[index];",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('currentOldPath', step.oldPath);",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('currentNewPath', step.newPath);",
              "    console.log('[' + (index + 1) + '/' + queue.length + '] Renaming: ' + step.oldPath);",
              "    console.log('                -> ' + step.newPath);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const queue = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('fileRenameQueue') || '[]');",
              "let index   = parseInt(pm.collectionVariables.get('fileRenameIndex') || '0', 10);",
              "",
              "// Guard: if somehow past the end, stop immediately",
              "if (index >= queue.length) {",
              "    console.log('Nothing left in queue — stopping runner.');",
                  "    pm.execution.setNextRequest(null);",
              "    return;",
              "}",
              "",
              "pm.test('[' + (index + 1) + '/' + queue.length + '] renameFile succeeded (200 OK)', () => {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "// Advance the counter",
              "index++;",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('fileRenameIndex', String(index));",
              "",
              "if (index < queue.length) {",
              "    // More files — loop back to this same request",
              "    pm.execution.setNextRequest('4. Rename Episode File (loop)');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    // All done",
                  "    console.log('');",
                  "    console.log('PART 2 COMPLETE — all ' + queue.length + ' episode files renamed.');",
                  "    console.log('Refresh the Content tab in qBittorrent if paths look stale.');",
                  "    pm.execution.setNextRequest(null);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "urlencoded",
          "urlencoded": [
            {
              "key": "hash",
              "value": "{{torrentHash}}",
              "description": "Torrent hash"
            },
            {
              "key": "oldPath",
              "value": "{{currentOldPath}}",
              "description": "Current file path — managed automatically by the loop"
            },
            {
              "key": "newPath",
              "value": "{{currentNewPath}}",
              "description": "New file path — managed automatically by the loop"
            }
          ]
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{qbtBaseUrl}}/api/v2/torrents/renameFile",
          "host": ["{{qbtBaseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "v2", "torrents", "renameFile"]
        },
        "description": "Renames one episode file per execution. The pre-request script loads the current item from {{fileRenameQueue}} using {{fileRenameIndex}} as the cursor. The test script increments the index and calls postman.setNextRequest() to loop back until the queue is exhausted.\n\nMUST be run via the Collection Runner — the Send button will only rename one file."
      }
    }
  ]
}
